From 2457bae0125a3a01f145f960185b365564823604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:52:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Limit fresh metadata execution to the visible key domain

Base: promoted vLLM tree ea1281f880e7535e3d87725be0156a8e38fc2fb2 plus the first eleven experiment patches. Rationale: the1M-planned-width/short-visibility diagnostic spends74% of kernel time rebuilding and bounding invisible metadata. This explicitly tests the producer/consumer interaction of a bounded512-CTA envelope grid over visible clusters and tensor bounds that skip invisible tiles/reads. Invisible metadata tails are deliberately unwritten; scalar bounds already skip them. Visible endpoints, conservative rounding allowance and all final scoring/handoff arithmetic are unchanged; no persistent state. Tests: visible-prefix endpoint oracle, fresh patch and source checks; full dense/source/grouped, native geometry, graph and strict sanitizer GPU gates pending. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
---
 .../tilelang/clustered_indexer.py             | 202 +++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 104 insertions(+), 98 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/clustered_indexer.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/clustered_indexer.py
index 52367edf37..e8cb6682e1 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/clustered_indexer.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/clustered_indexer.py
